Report the source text the parser did not read.

Beautiful Mermaid's line-at-a-time parsers are total. Every statement they
cannot read has a defined silent reading: the flowchart's `consumeNode` falls
back to `BARE_NODE_REGEX` and takes the leading word, `parseEdgeLine` drops
whatever it could not advance past, and `parseStateDiagram`'s loop falls off the
end of its last pattern. So the graph they hand back cannot tell a statement
that was read from one that was guessed, and a host has nothing to check: a
source this renderer does not implement draws a box labelled with its own id
beside a node nobody wrote, with no error anywhere.

This records the text each parser walked away from, on the graph it returns, and
exports one function that answers it for a whole source. No statement reads
differently and no drawing changes; a source the parser reads whole reports an
empty list. The leftovers are the parser's own — it is the only thing that knows
what it read — which is why this is a patch to it rather than a grammar written
beside it.

Leaf's own, not upstream's. It goes away when a release carries the reading:
delete this file and the `unreadMermaidText` export in `vendor.py`'s entry, and
`lf-diagram.js` keeps calling the same name. The same silence is behind
lukilabs/beautiful-mermaid#140, where `A-->B` draws one node named `A--`.

